From: picture-frame build
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: enable the I-cache in enable_caches()

With CONFIG_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT (U-Boot started by the Rockchip
miniloader on the RK3126), start.S never enables the I-cache, so U-Boot
ran with it off: code with many instructions per byte (e.g. a DRAM test
loop) was 6-8 times slower.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
@@ -210,7 +210,12 @@
 #if !defined(CONFIG_SYS_DCACHE_OFF) && !defined(CONFIG_ARM64)
 void enable_caches(void)
 {
-	/* Enable D-cache. I-cache is already enabled in start.S */
+	/*
+	 * start.S only enables the I-cache in cpu_init_cp15, which
+	 * CONFIG_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT skips (U-Boot started by the Rockchip
+	 * miniloader): enable it here, it is a no-op when already on
+	 */
+	icache_enable();
 	dcache_enable();
 }
 #endif
